yload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root causes, 2026-11-12 PST, each reproduced deterministically.\n1. test_bridge_sync_honours_an_active_pause: the ref lock's local git bound (_ref_lock._LOCAL_TIMEOUT_SECS = 5.0 s, a fail-closed production policy) turns a starved host into a correct \"treat as HELD\" verdict. Reproduced by injecting a timeout into any `git rev-parse --verify` bounded under 6 s: same error text as the sighting. Fix (commit in this ticket's change): the module's stub_pass fixture raises the bound to 60 s for these semantics tests only, following bug ddc8's precedent in tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock.py; the production bound is untouched. All 5 module tests pass with the injected slow git.\n2. test_cli_passed_but_unsigned_is_exit_11_with_byte_identical_stderr: the failure itself was \"--- Logging error --- ... ValueError: I/O operation on closed file\", the stale stderr handler fixed by bald-diagnostic-cricket (a9300a8b2f2). The `Errno 48 ... address already in use` line was misattributed: in the original log (salvaged fix-haddock make-verify.log, port 55506) it is the PytestUnhandledThreadExceptionWarning from tests/unit/test_audit_serve.py::test_await_listening_reports_a_server_that_cannot_bind, which binds a held port deliberately and passed. On current main the facade test passes 3 of 3 with a stderr handler installed under a since-closed stream plus a warning emitted during the test (the exact failing condition). No port is bound by the facade test; nothing to fix there.","timestamp":1794478957752856634},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-12 06:00 PST: in_progress. Fix committed in .rebar/worktrees/fix-tuna as 0ba4ed1814f, not pushed (root causes and reproductions in the comment above). Next: make verify, push, close after the Bedrock spend cap releases (16:00 PST).","timestamp":1794491832116261862},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-12 PST: CLOSED (class preexisting, completion signature signed). Change 3379 merged as ef707f4ad0c. Plan review and close ran through the worktree CLI on the Anthropic API (anthropic:claude-sonnet-5-5) while the Bedrock spend cap held.","timestamp":1794524321398320001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1793830821694917001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"256dc0ef-1c10-48c9-bfcc-aa252c7b9dc1","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9018-3385-ccfa-4568"},{"link_uuid":"53076223-b261-49bc-84c6-59a902585c17","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"dfcc-d11b-fc0f-40e0"},{"link_uuid":"d6cc0fb8-7bb2-4b94-8d8b-162b4ca83522","provenance":"derived","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"f75f-5d85-7b9a-4d86"}],"description":"## Observation\nDuring `make verify` at 1bfa37ca141 with host load average about 44, 2 tests failed and then passed 3 of 3 in isolation: `tests/interfaces/store/test_bridge_sync_holds_ref_lock.py::test_bridge_sync_honours_an_active_pause` (`cannot pause bridge: git rev-parse --verify timed out after 5.0s (fail-closed: treat as HELD)`) and `tests/interfaces/facades/test_plan_review_attestation_facades.py::test_cli_passed_but_unsigned_is_exit_11_with_byte_identical_stderr` (`OSError: [Errno 48] ... address already in use` binding 127.0.0.1:55506).\n\n## Expected\nNeither test depends on host load: no fixed 5 s subprocess budget in a test path, and no fixed or reused loopback port.\n\n## Testing\n\n`pytest tests/interfaces/store/test_bridge_sync_holds_ref_lock.py` passes with every local `git rev-parse --verify` under 6 s forced to time out (the reproduction), and the facade test passes with a stderr handler installed under a closed stream.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Each failure is reproduced deterministically (injected slow git; a pre-bound port) and fixed at its class.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_bridge_sync_holds_ref_lock.py","reason":"local git bound headroom for semantics tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","dfcc-d11b-fc0f-40e0"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"cea1f51d-fff2-4570-8805-84d2aa43c35b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"8e6c-3a37-8570-4e82","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Two tests fail under host load: a 5 s git timeout and a fixed loopback port","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["734a891f-7ed0-4965-b4ba-50c042c462f4","1335a88b-61f9-45c8-b777-84f8c0fb84f6","c7f839bc-c723-4926-8f9e-c3d9573d5c32","041a1a5f-4a2a-47fe-bed6-a6dd8b1535e1","8cd6b209-7856-4c90-81d3-c313b0831b2f","53076223-b261-49bc-84c6-59a902585c17","80aecf8a-f715-44ef-9ff3-2ccef1f5b2c5","49bf66e9-34d1-4bc0-bce4-5b37d6287b39","516b71d6-f814-4480-924f-8185826c535d","cea1f51d-fff2-4570-8805-84d2aa43c35b","207daefc-438d-4a42-bb25-ec60310597f0","d6cc0fb8-7bb2-4b94-8d8b-162b4ca83522","9156e95d-51c7-4d7e-89bd-a5fc77edb6c6"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794524321398320002,"uuid":"67090395-cf29-419f-a5d6-4e5d759baa0f"}